RDMA/bnxt_re: Free CQ toggle page after firmware teardown

jira KERNEL-1952
cve CVE-2026-72499
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.26.1.el9_9
commit-author Selvin Xavier <selvin.xavier@broadcom.com>
commit bb45e06f9914ca64ac95341a80a0c20bb8dd46a9
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.26.1.el9_9/bb45e06f.failed

Free the toggle page only after firmware teardown completes so that
an NQ interrupt arriving during bnxt_qplib_destroy_cq() won't write
the toggle value to an already-freed page. Move free_page() after
bnxt_qplib_destroy_cq.

Fixes: e275919d9669 ("RDMA/bnxt_re: Share a page to expose per CQ info with userspace")
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/r/20260615224751.232802-4-selvin.xavier@broadcom.com
	Signed-off-by: Selvin Xavier <selvin.xavier@broadcom.com>
	Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit bb45e06f9914ca64ac95341a80a0c20bb8dd46a9)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/infiniband/hw/bnxt_re/ib_verbs.c
diff --cc drivers/infiniband/hw/bnxt_re/ib_verbs.c
index 5aabce9ac606,35905ae7d168..000000000000
--- a/drivers/infiniband/hw/bnxt_re/ib_verbs.c
+++ b/drivers/infiniband/hw/bnxt_re/ib_verbs.c
@@@ -3060,14 -3468,17 +3060,23 @@@ int bnxt_re_destroy_cq(struct ib_cq *ib
  	nq = cq->qplib_cq.nq;
  	cctx = rdev->chip_ctx;
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	if (cctx->modes.toggle_bits & BNXT_QPLIB_CQ_TOGGLE_BIT) {
 +		free_page((unsigned long)cq->uctx_cq_page);
++=======
+ 	ret = ib_is_udata_in_empty(udata);
+ 	if (ret)
+ 		return ret;
+ 
+ 	if (cctx->modes.toggle_bits & BNXT_QPLIB_CQ_TOGGLE_BIT)
++>>>>>>> bb45e06f9914 (RDMA/bnxt_re: Free CQ toggle page after firmware teardown)
  		hash_del(&cq->hash_entry);
- 	}
  	bnxt_qplib_destroy_cq(&rdev->qplib_res, &cq->qplib_cq);
+ 	if (cctx->modes.toggle_bits & BNXT_QPLIB_CQ_TOGGLE_BIT)
+ 		free_page((unsigned long)cq->uctx_cq_page);
  
  	bnxt_re_put_nq(rdev, nq);
 +	ib_umem_release(cq->umem);
  
  	atomic_dec(&rdev->stats.res.cq_count);
  	kfree(cq->cql);
* Unmerged path drivers/infiniband/hw/bnxt_re/ib_verbs.c
